A("Phase six: one stock, one hype.",PH(6,"One stock, one hype",40))
A("Mistake number five: putting everything on one stock, one sector, or one hype. It feels exciting when it works. It is brutal when it does not.",I("right",40,"chips",**ch(["One stock","flag","stock"],["One sector","gear","sector"],["One hype","bolt","hype"],title="Mistake #5")))
A("Even great companies can lose most of their value, and some go to zero. Enron and Lehman Brothers were both giants, and both ended in bankruptcy.",I("left",39,"chips",**ch(["Enron","warn","Enron"],["Lehman Brothers","bank","Lehman"],["Both: bankruptcy","cross","bankruptcy"],title="Giants can fall")))
A("Now the surprising part. Finance professor Hendrik Bessembinder studied almost twenty-six thousand US stocks from nineteen twenty-six to twenty sixteen. Only about four percent of them created all of the net wealth above Treasury bills.",dict(type="dots",img=45,title="US stocks, 1926–2016",groups=[[4,"gold","≈ 4 % created all the net wealth","four"],[96,"grey","everything else","everything"]],big="4 %",bigcol="gold",foot="H. Bessembinder, Arizona State University"))
A("Fifty-eight percent of stocks did not even beat Treasury bills over their lifetimes.",dict(type="dots",img=45,title="US stocks, 1926–2016",groups=[[58,"red","Did not beat T-bills","Fifty-eight"],[38,"grey","Moderate gains","bills"],[4,"gold","Big winners","bills"]],big="58 %",bigcol="red",foot="H. Bessembinder, Arizona State University"))
A("So picking one stock means betting that you found one of the rare winners. Owning many stocks means you own the winners automatically, even if you cannot name them in advance.",I("right",45,"vs",title="Two ways to bet",a=["One stock","lottery ticket","red","betting"],b=["Many stocks","own the winners","green","automatically"]))
A("That is what diversification means. Not a fancy trick, just spreading your money across hundreds or thousands of companies, ideally across industries and countries. A broad index fund does that in a single purchase.",I("left",44,"chips",**ch(["Hundreds of companies","house","hundreds"],["Many industries","gear","industries"],["Many countries","globe","countries"],["One purchase: index fund","check","single"],title="Diversification")))
A("Be careful with tips on social media, too. The person on screen may be paid to promote something, may already own the stock, and you rarely see their losing trades.",I("right",57,"chips",**ch(["Paid to promote?","coin","paid"],["Already own it?","lens","own"],["Losses stay hidden","cross","losing"],title="Before you follow a tip")))
A("A simple test: if someone says it is guaranteed, urgent, or a secret, walk away. Real investing is slow, public, and a little bit boring.",I("left",58,"stamp",text="Guaranteed? Urgent? Secret?",sub="walk away",col="red"))
