A("Phase eight: the boring plan.",PH(8,"The boring plan",19))
A("So what do people do instead? Here is what many educational sources suggest, not advice for you personally. First: build an emergency fund, and pay off expensive debt.",I("right",28,"chips",**ch(["Emergency fund","shield","emergency"],["Pay off costly debt","cross","debt"],title="Step 1")))
A("Second: money for the long term, ten years or more, often goes into low-cost, broadly diversified funds.",I("left",19,"chips",**ch(["10+ years","clock","ten"],["Low-cost","pct","low"],["Broadly diversified","globe","diversified"],title="Step 2")))
A("Third: invest regularly, for example every month, so you never have to guess the perfect moment.",I("right",47,"chips",**ch(["Every month","cal","month"],["No perfect moment","clock","guess"],["Fewer decisions","check","fewer"],title="Step 3")))
A("Fourth: write down your plan, and check your portfolio rarely. Looking at it every day mostly makes you nervous.",I("left",27,"chips",**ch(["Written plan","doc","write"],["Check rarely","cal","rarely"],title="Step 4")))
A("And fifth: keep learning, and be honest about what you do not know. If your situation is complicated, a licensed advisor can help.",I("right",31,"chips",**ch(["Keep learning","bulb","learning"],["Know your limits","lens","honest"],["Complicated? Ask a pro","heart","complicated"],title="Step 5")))
A("None of this is exciting. And that is the point. Boring is what makes it work.",I("full",15,"stamp",text="Boring works",sub="",col="gold"))
