A("Phase nine: the honest answer.",PH(9,"The honest answer",52))
A("So, what should you never do with your money when you invest? Never invest money you need soon. Never invest borrowed money or gamble. Never ignore fees. Never panic sell. And never put everything on one stock or one hype.",I("right",52,"five",icon="cross",items=["Money you need soon","Borrowed money & gambling","Ignoring fees","Panic selling","All-in on one bet"],t=["soon","borrowed","ignore","panic","everything"],title="Never do this"))
A("Will avoiding them make you rich quickly? No. There are no guarantees in investing, and markets can still fall. But you give yourself the best chance, because you stay in the game.",I("left",29,"chips",**ch(["No quick riches","cross","quickly"],["No guarantees","warn","guarantees"],["You stay in the game","shield","stay"],title="The honest answer")))
A("Remember, this video is for education only. It is not financial advice. I do not know your situation or your goals, so do your own research, or talk to a licensed professional.",I("full",28,"stamp",text="Education only",sub="not financial advice",col="gold"))
